  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd the AI workflow guide under Automate. Preserve the guide/ai/ URL as an alias.\nLink the guide from both indexes and the MCP reference.\nDocument cloud providers, Ollama, credentials, offline mode and external MCP clients.\nState the current panel limits for Unsloth Studio, LM Studio and llama-server.\nGive four worked CAM tasks with 20 JSON-RPC tool calls.\nExplain selection, warnings, Undo Turn, posting approval, privacy and connection failures.\nFollow the latest issue scope. Leave #1944 and #1947 outside this pass.\nRecord the choices in docs/decisions/1949-ai-guide.md.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe full AI workflow guide was missing.\nThe MCP page still said that the panel had no live transport.\nThe native transport now ships. The panel exposes fewer endpoints than the provider library.\n\nRead the shipped panel controls, presets, HTTP transport, credential lookup and keychain code.\nCheck CLI help, the MCP port parser, tool schemas, selection replies and verification findings.\nCheck the Pocket kind and feed parameter against the command and parameter code.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll five pins fail before the guide changes and pass after them:\n\n- test_provider_setup_and_shipped_limits\n- test_external_agents_and_four_worked_tasks\n- test_indexes_and_mcp_page_link_the_guide\n- ai_guide_calls_match_live_tools_list\n- ai_guide_camcraft_flags_match_parsers\n\nRun the Python pins with:\n`python3 -B -m unittest discover -s site/tests -p test_ai_guide.py`.\nRun the Rust pins with `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test ai_guide`.\n\nThe Rust test calls tools/list through the live MCP server.\nIt checks example tool names, argument keys, required arguments and inline tool names.\nThe flag test checks CamCraft MCP help and the actual UI port parser.\nThe llama-server flag belongs to that external runtime.\n\nMutation checks restore each old guide file separately:\n\n- Remove the new automate/ai.md page: red, then green after restoration.\n- Restore guide/_index.md from upstream/main: red, then green after restoration.\n- Restore automate/_index.md from upstream/main: red, then green after restoration.\n- Restore automate/mcp.md from upstream/main: red, then green after restoration.\n\nRemoving the new page also makes both Rust pins fail. Restoring it makes both pass.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes the app ai_guide suite.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\nZola 0.23.6 builds 48 pages and 10 sections with no orphan pages.\nAll five existing guide navigation tests pass.\n`git diff --check` passes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff for .nc and .cl files is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo live provider credentials, provider network calls or external agent installations were used.\nNo interactive GUI or physical machine workflow was run.\nThe tests validate documentation and tool schemas. They do not prove a sample CAM job safe.\nThe unsupported local panel setup routes remain explicit limits.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2924 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes the MCP tools table. This change updates the AI Chat transport paragraph.\nNo stack is needed.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1949\n",
